          "text": "Hello,\n\n**History of Present Illness:**  \nThe patient has genetic generalized epilepsy with typical absence seizures, beginning at age 13. Current seizure frequency is approximately two seizures per month. The epilepsy is drug responsive.\n\n**Current Medications:**  \n- Lamotrigine  \n- Lacosamide  \n\n**Seizure Burden:**  \nTypical absence seizures occurring approximately twice monthly.\n\n**Assessment:**  \nGenetic generalized epilepsy with typical absence seizures, associated with a pathogenic PCDH19 variant, c.918G>A. Brain MRI demonstrates nonspecific white matter changes. Epilepsy remains drug responsive on the current antiseizure medication regimen.\n\n**Plan:**  \n- Continue lamotrigine and lacosamide.  \n- Continue monitoring seizure frequency.  \n- Follow up in the epilepsy clinic.",
